{
  "$comment": "Tube product catalogue (v3). Shapes list their diameters and sizes; closures list where they fit (compat: shape → diameter → chart|confirm) and the colour families they come in there (colours: shape → diameter → ids). Sizes, compat and colours are imported from the Arapoush size charts (OPEX → Catalogue import, or `pnpm --filter @arapoush/opex-api tube:chart`). `aliases` are the chart wordings that map onto an entry. `model` is the 3D family (`param`: the parametric cap, shaped by `shape3d` in ratios of the tube radius); `shoulder` swaps the tube shoulder (eye-nozzle caps). Structures may be limited to shapes, diameters or closures. Samples are ranked by how well their tags match the selection. Prints are a sample (one row per method on page.printing, every shape and diameter) until the client sends its print chart; bodyColours and the coloured palette are operator data.",
  "version": 3,
  "updated": "2026-11-12",
